{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Upon</b> — as though they would carry you upon palms." "The vav [in תשאנו] is dotted — on account of the regular form, in the manner of: <i>For your covenant is with the stones of the field</i>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 91, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra appears to address why the normal spelling (with vav) would be 'struck' (דגוש/dotted); the integration of the two phrases is unclear in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:57.627624634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}